# Social Provider Integration Guidelines

When adding a new social media provider integration, follow these guidelines to maintain consistency and reliability across the application.

## 1. Callback Route Structure

Create a new callback route in `apps/app/app/api/callback/[provider]/route.ts`:

```typescript
// Required imports
import { getAuth } from '@delulu/auth/server';
import { database } from '@delulu/database';
import type { NextRequest } from 'next/server';
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { env } from '@/env';
import { nanoid } from 'nanoid';

// Define provider-specific interfaces
interface ProviderResponse {
  access_token: string;
  refresh_token?: string; // Optional, not all providers give refresh tokens
  expires_in: number;
}

interface ProviderUserResponse {
  // Define user profile fields
}

// Use consistent timeout
const TIMEOUT_MS = 8000;

// Reuse fetchWithTimeout helper
async function fetchWithTimeout(url: string, options: RequestInit, timeout = TIMEOUT_MS) {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const id = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeout);
  try {
    const response = await fetch(url, {
      ...options,
      signal: controller.signal,
    });
    clearTimeout(id);
    return response;
  } catch (error) {
    clearTimeout(id);
    throw error;
  }
}
```

## 2. Error Handling

Use consistent error types and codes:

```typescript
// Error redirect format
new URL(
  `/socials?error=${errorType}&code=${PROVIDER}_ERR&provider=${PROVIDER}`,
  env.NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL
);

// Common error types
const errors = {
  auth_required: 'AUTH_001',
  invalid_request: 'PARAM_001',
  provider_auth_failed: `${PROVIDER}_001`,
  token_invalid: `${PROVIDER}_002`,
  user_fetch_failed: `${PROVIDER}_003`,
};
```

## 3. Database Integration

Follow this pattern for social provider data:

```typescript
await database.socialProvider.upsert({
  where: {
    userId_profileId: {
      userId,
      profileId: userObject.id,
    },
  },
  create: {
    id: `social_${nanoid(12)}`,
    accessToken: access_token,
    refreshToken, // If available
    expiresIn: new Date(Date.now() + expires_in * 1000),
    fullName: '', // Provider-specific name format
    username: '', // Provider-specific username
    profileImage: '', // Provider-specific image URL
    profileId: userObject.id,
    userId,
    socialType: 'PROVIDER_TYPE',
    isActive: true,
    lastSyncedAt: new Date(),
  },
  update: {
    // Similar fields as create
    updatedAt: new Date(),
  },
});
```

## 4. Environment Variables

Add required environment variables in `.env`:

```bash
# Provider OAuth credentials
PROVIDER_CLIENT_ID=
PROVIDER_CLIENT_SECRET=
PROVIDER_CALLBACK_URL=
```

## 5. Update Notifications

Add provider-specific messages in `social-notifications.tsx`:

```typescript
const ERROR_MESSAGES = {
  [`${provider}_auth_failed`]: {
    title: 'Authentication Failed',
    description: 'We encountered an error while connecting. Please try again.',
  },
  // ... other error types
};

const NOTIFICATIONS = {
  account_transferred: {
    title: `${Provider} Account Transferred`,
    description: 'Your account was successfully transferred.',
  },
};
```

## 6. Testing Checklist

Before deploying a new provider:

1. ✅ Verify OAuth flow works
2. ✅ Test error scenarios
3. ✅ Verify account transfer flow
4. ✅ Check token expiration handling
5. ✅ Test retry functionality
6. ✅ Verify notifications display correctly

## 7. Security Considerations

1. Always use HTTPS for API calls
2. Never expose OAuth credentials in client-side code
3. Validate all incoming data
4. Use timeouts for external API calls
5. Implement rate limiting
6. Handle token expiration gracefully
